WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:04.500
Yeah, back to staring at a static background.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.930
We had a little something planned 
for this segment, but, y'know?

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:12.180
And these lines were recorded three 
days before the episode aired.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:16.350
I'm sure that the clever members of the 
Gintama audience can figure out what happened.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:21.000
So here's another episode of 
Gintama, living on the edge.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.990
Okay, so the comments here were also written
 at the last minute the day before the episode aired

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:01.990
The Lions won the Pacific League.
No idea who won the Central League since they're still playing.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:05.100
<b>Don't Look</b>

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:04.500
Don't look.

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:09.980
I found this in Elizabeth's room.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:13.980
What is it that I'm not supposed to look for?

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.390
Or does it count as looking 
when I'm looking for what it is

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:20.830
that I'm not supposed to be looking for?

00:02:20.830 --> 00:02:24.070
In that case, I'll have to look for someone to look

00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:26.810
for what I'm not supposed to look for,

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.950
before deciding if I should 
look or if I should not look.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:31.530
So I'm looking for someone who's 
willing to look for the answer.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.750
But if I'm not supposed to look,

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.500
then I can't look for the someone to look for the

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.010
someone to look for the someone to look for the...

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:40.340
You're making this too hard.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:43.770
It's like you're lost in a 
maze of what not to look for.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.210
Don't look...

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.220
I won't.

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.020
It's pretty obvious what this is.

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.480
He ran away from home.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:52.230
E-Elizabeth ran away from home?!

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:54.290
I-Impossible! Unfathomable!

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:57.610
He had no reason to be unhappy!

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.230
The last time I saw Elizabeth...

00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:01.900
The last time I...

00:03:01.900 --> 00:03:03.630
Th-The last...

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.070
When was the last time I saw Elizabeth?

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.410
You can't remember?!

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.110
I thought you noticed as 
soon as he disappeared?

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:12.750
No...

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:20.020
<b>Zura: We have a testimonial from Mrs. 
E who was able to find her happiness.</b>

00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:16.350
Two episodes ago, when I was 
writing that text message,

00:03:16.350 --> 00:03:18.530
I didn't recognize who was in the picture.

00:03:18.530 --> 00:03:20.010
That's why he ran away from home!

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.040
There's a tiny date on the sign.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.760
That means he was still around then.

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:26.420
Huh?

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:27.780
What day is today?

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:29.770
October 31st.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:31.420
I would understand if 
he put yesterday's date,

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:32.710
but why is it tomorrow's date?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.800
The sign must be from the future!

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.110
That can't be it.

00:03:36.110 --> 00:03:37.270
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.030
Go the other direction.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.800
Maybe that's a year old?

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:42.630
Huh?

00:03:43.150 --> 00:03:44.770
Now that I think about it, it's been

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:47.030
a while since I've actually seen him in person.

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.260
Wh-What do you mean?!

00:03:49.260 --> 00:03:52.040
E-Elizabeth ran away from home a year ago?!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:55.880
And I went about my life without a clue?!

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.290
You're the one who can't remember.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.350
Don't be ridiculous!

00:03:58.350 --> 00:04:01.230
You heartless bastards may have forgotten,

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.300
but how could I have 
forgotten about Elizabeth?!

00:04:03.630 --> 00:04:05.640
That's absurd!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.270
Damn, I can't remember!

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.530
For some reason, my memories 
of Elizabeth are so erratic!

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:12.810
Have they ever not been?

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:18.820
What happened between us, Elizabeth?!

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.770
<b>Tenny's</b>

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:23.820
<b>The People You Tend to Forget Tend 
to Shop Up After You Forget Them</b>

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:28.090
We must locate Elizabeth at once.

00:04:28.090 --> 00:04:29.910
But my memory is hazy.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:33.350
I won't be able to remember 
anything in the past.

00:04:33.350 --> 00:04:34.290
That is why...

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:38.660
It's not Zura, it's Katsura.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.550
Uh, nobody said anything.

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:42.420
What are these, Zura?

00:04:42.710 --> 00:04:44.460
It's not Zura, it's a sign.

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:49.680
<b>You little girls should 
go home and watch Ainori!!</b>

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:46.050
Does this look familiar?

00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:49.680
That was Elizabeth's line from 
the popularity contest arc.

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:54.790
Yes, all of the signs he's 
used are stored here.

00:04:54.790 --> 00:04:56.700
We can use these to determine why he ran

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:58.940
away from home, and his current location as well.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.940
Hey, I don't have time to 
dig through all of these.

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.350
This is the only lead we have.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:05.310
Don't worry.

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.490
Elizabeth was a samurai at heart.

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:08.980
He only spoke when necessary.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:11.450
For example, look at how this 
line is short and simple.

00:05:11.450 --> 00:05:15.710
<b>No, could be anyone.</b>

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:14.540
Uh, who was he talking to 
and what was trying to say?

00:05:14.540 --> 00:05:15.710
It's very simple.

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:16.950
This is...

00:05:16.950 --> 00:05:18.210
Is it an echo?

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.420
<b>No, could be anyone.</b>

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.420
<b>No, could be anyone.</b>

00:05:21.430 --> 00:05:22.420
How the hell were we supposed to know that?!

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:26.160
Every time we saw this commercial,

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:30.270
he would raise this sign and I would go "OC"!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.390
But now I hear nothing...

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:33.690
How is he a samurai at heart?!

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:34.810
Elizabeth...

00:05:33.690 --> 00:05:35.930
We're supposed to go through 
all of these stupid signs?!

00:05:36.290 --> 00:05:39.250
Is there anything that looks suspicious?

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:40.860
Oh, this is...

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:43.390
<b>Thank you.</b>

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:42.690
He suddenly said thank you.

00:05:43.150 --> 00:05:45.220
And look at the next one.

00:05:43.390 --> 00:05:47.850
<b>Goodbye.</b>

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:47.230
This was when he decided to leave.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:48.170
What lead to these signs?

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:52.350
...will bring you lots of scary friends...

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.220
Pop, pop, pop!

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.990
AC again?!

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.410
Every time we saw this commercial,

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:02.600
we would take turns on the bunny and Lionel Richie parts.

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:05.510
If you don't cut this out, I'm gonna 
Goodbye Lionel Richie your ass!

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:05.510
Elizabeth...

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.090
Hey, these are all related to commercials!

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:06.930
<b>No, it's kefir.</b>

00:06:06.930 --> 00:06:08.180
<b>No, it's Yayataka.</b>

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.480
How much TV do you watch?!

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:08.930
<b>No, it's Pitts.</b>

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:09.810
<b>No, it's Boss.</b>

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:11.010
Aren't the Joi supposed to 
be taking back the country?!

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:11.020
<b>No, it's Ondroid.</b>

00:06:11.380 --> 00:06:13.510
These are the only decent ones.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.340
Excuse me, your collar is turned up.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.380
Was your hair done at the same 
place where Tokiko Gato goes?

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.560
How do you write out Renho?

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:23.060
They're all about Renho!

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:26.240
And when did he use these signs?!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:28.600
Doesn't this mean he was talking to Renho?!

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.310
Was your hair done at the same place?

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:35.260
I'm close to remembering something.

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.260
I believe this line was when...

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:43.980
Yes, it was a winter day that 
left you cold in body and soul.

00:06:43.980 --> 00:06:44.810
No, stop!

00:06:44.810 --> 00:06:47.170
Don't start a flashback 
from those stupid lines!

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:51.290
We were on the run, without 
a roof above our heads.

00:06:51.290 --> 00:06:53.090
Hey! I said to stop!

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.320
This race pits the young

00:06:55.320 --> 00:06:58.570
Renho against the older Ishihara in a one-on-one duel!

00:06:58.570 --> 00:06:59.950
You're watching TV again?!

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.220
Just end this!

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:03.690
Say something funny about 
Renho's hair and end this!

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.950
I see, so these two are...

00:07:05.950 --> 00:07:07.650
Don't bother setting up the joke!

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:08.870
Look at Renho's hair!

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:11.160
She must go to the same 
place Tokiko Gato goes!

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.980
Is Ishihara the one who can provide 
hope in these times of trouble?

00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:16.180
Or is it Renho?

00:07:16.630 --> 00:07:17.790
Which one is the answer?

00:07:17.850 --> 00:07:21.560
<b>No, it's Katsura.</b>

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.900
Another OC commercial?!

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:22.530
Wait! You're not going to say anything?!

00:07:22.530 --> 00:07:25.000
You're not going to comment on Renho's hair?!

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:30.890
Idle chatter did little to stave 
off the biting cold and hunger.

00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:33.140
Stop wasting time on this 
pointless flashback!

00:07:33.140 --> 00:07:37.900
I couldn't die here before starting 
a revolution in this country.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:41.830
As we dragged ourselves 
along, that was when...

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:45.970
<b>Renho</b>

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.040
Make Renho your first choice.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.600
Make Renho your second choice.

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:47.520
Renho is more than number one.

00:07:45.620 --> 00:07:47.720
Hey! It's the real Renho!

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:49.560
Renho is the only one.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:48.480
Look at that hair!

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:49.530
Her collars are turned way up!

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.360
You can use all of your signs now!

00:07:51.360 --> 00:07:54.520
I see, you ignored the previous opportunity 
so you could use them all here!

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.370
Are you okay?

00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:58.770
I can carry that for you.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.930
Forget about the old lady!

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.160
Look at that hair behind you! Say something!

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.180
Thank you.

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:07.700
There are still kind souls left in Edo.

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:08.880
Yeah, very nice!

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.920
But it would be even better if 
he ended this stupid flashback!

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:15.290
That was when we met Grandma Fumiko.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.930
Uh, nobody cares about the old lady!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.880
Grandma Fumiko would tell picture stories to

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:23.130
the children in the park at the top of the stairs.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.700
You've completely lost your chance!

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:26.560
You're never going to get a better shot!

00:08:26.770 --> 00:08:30.470
In this age, kids don't 
care about picture stories.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:34.280
Yet Grandma Fumiko would climb the stairs

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.820
every day with her heavy load.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:42.830
Maybe that was why Elizabeth began 
visiting the park every day.

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:45.770
Damn! This is turning into one 
of those heartwarming stories!

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:47.580
Renho's never coming back!

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:49.550
When it was raining...

00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.890
When it was windy...

00:08:53.240 --> 00:08:54.420
When it was Renho...

00:08:54.420 --> 00:08:55.760
There's Renho!

00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.750
Elizabeth went to the park with Grandma Fumiko

00:08:59.750 --> 00:09:02.610
every day to watch the kids play.

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.570
It's a miracle!

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:06.230
Renho is back with her funky hair!

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.380
Er, wait.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:08.360
Renho's eating something!

00:09:08.570 --> 00:09:09.960
Gin-san! It's fried chicken!

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:12.970
One day, Elizabeth finally asked Grandma 
Fumiko the question that had been bugging him.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:11.580
Renho's eating fried chicken!

00:09:11.580 --> 00:09:13.110
Hey, look behind you!

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:13.870
Say something!

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:16.090
Funky chick eating fried chicken!

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:18.370
<b>Why do you come here every day?</b>

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.370
You think it's strange?

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:24.620
A storyteller spends all day watching 
the children instead of telling stories?

00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:25.210
It's no use!

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.490
The fried chicken doesn't help!
 They aren't looking!

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:28.130
Hey!

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:30.410
Renho is throwing fried chicken at them!

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:31.940
But they still haven't noticed her!

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:35.630
I tell stories to make the children smile.

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.710
But look, they're having 
plenty of fun already.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:45.520
So my job is to watch over them.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.150
Renho's messing up her hair in front of them!

00:09:48.430 --> 00:09:54.900
<b>I want to see your picture story.</b>

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:51.830
You're such a strange one.

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:54.900
If he doesn't use those signs now,
 he's never gonna use them!

00:09:55.670 --> 00:10:00.170
Oh, well. I suppose I can tell 
you one of my best stories.

00:10:00.170 --> 00:10:02.910
Please! End this flashback!

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:09.180
<b>Was your hair done at the same 
place where Tokiko Gato goes?</b>

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:06.610
Let's begin then.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:11.980
The story of "Was your hair done at the 
same place where Tokiko Gato goes?"

00:10:11.980 --> 00:10:13.170
There?!

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:14.610
You can use it there?!

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:15.480
Wait!

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:18.430
After all that buildup, it 
wasn't even Elizabeth's sign?!

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:20.810
It has nothing to do with Renho, you a-hole!

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:23.190
And what kind of picture story is this?!

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.930
No wonder the kids stayed away!

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.580
I can't remember the details...

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:33.680
I wasn't paying attention so I can't 
remember anything after the title.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.690
Was it that scary?!

00:10:35.690 --> 00:10:40.050
But why does Elizabeth have a 
sign from the granny's story?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:44.080
I have a feeling that this 
line will help me remember.

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:46.310
<b>Excuse me, your collar is turned up.</b>

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.500
No, no more!

00:10:45.500 --> 00:10:47.100
Just stop!

00:10:47.380 --> 00:10:48.830
I believe this line was when...

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.920
He started another flashback!

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:53.940
Please get to the point and make this short!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.560
Eli, you were too much.

00:10:56.970 --> 00:11:01.970
<b>Excuse me, your collar 
(my penis) is turned up.</b>

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:00.170
My back can't take it.

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:01.970
That was too short!

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.590
How did that even happen?!

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:05.770
What went down between them?!

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.470
You wasted all that time 
on the first flashback!

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:11.030
It isn't proper for us to probe 
into the affairs of other couples.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.730
All I can say is that Elizabeth isn't picky.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:15.510
This isn't a matter of being picky or not!

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.480
And where were you watching this from?!

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:20.220
<b>How do you write out Renho?</b>

00:11:17.620 --> 00:11:18.410
Wait!

00:11:18.410 --> 00:11:20.110
There's only one sign left!

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:23.040
Hey, Zura! What's wrong?!

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:24.620
My head...

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.410
I-I have a feeling

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.220
that I'm not supposed 
to remember what comes next...

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:31.310
Wait!

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:34.000
Don't tell me that you're talking about 
Elizabeth and the old lady getting down and dirty!

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:38.090
The flashback started! It started!

00:11:41.850 --> 00:11:45.520
Snow... It's so cold...

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:52.100
<b>Hold on.</b>

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:49.020
It's okay. Don't overdo it.

00:11:49.570 --> 00:11:52.100
You'll end up catching a cold.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.850
Besides...

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:57.360
I have my own.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.420
I'm sure that you've seen 
through my disguise.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.360
I may be wearing the skin 
of an earthling right now,

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:13.540
but you could never forget 
your former lover, could you?

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:20.090
But you could never forget 
your former lover, could you?

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:26.600
<b>B Part</b>

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:23.960
Or did you approach me 
because you recognized me?

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:26.600
So you could dispose of the traitor?

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:31.850
I was surprised to see that you were still 
using those signs to lie to yourself.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:35.340
After watching the people 
on this planet smile,

00:12:35.340 --> 00:12:37.520
I discovered my true calling.

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:41.820
I want to tell stories and protect 
the smiles of the people here.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:44.500
That is how I truly feel.

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.730
Don't you feel the same way?

